# Opinion

Meeting: 0003-improve-the-design-and-aesthetics-of-rps-arena
Agent: Critic
Task: Improve the design and aesthetics of RPS Arena
Context:
- UI refresh introduces new styling, typography, and rendering helpers without changing API routes or introducing a build step.
- Instructions prohibit screenshots/Playwright; quality enforced via c8 100% coverage and repo-wide pytest run.
- Static serving remains via Node HTTP server; adding Google Fonts introduces an external request.

Position:
- Design uplift is meaningful (sticky nav, stat grid, refined cards), but ensure accessibility (contrast/focus) remains acceptable with darker gradients.
- Google Fonts dependency is acceptable for aesthetics, but be mindful of offline scenarios; keep font stack with system fallbacks.
- Sanitization via render helpers is positive, yet we must ensure server-side still defends against malicious inputs (unchanged this round).

Recommendations:
- Verify focus states remain visible on ghost buttons and inputs after new border/glow styles; adjust if user reports issues.
- Consider adding a local font fallback or preconnect hints already included to mitigate font loading delays.
- Keep an eye on payload size of added CSS; if styles grow further, consider structuring into sections to maintain readability.
